# One heap holds two instances of the image, as under `bun test --isolate`, where each test file gets a fresh realm of one VM and `Bun.s3` carries what a file hangs on it to the next: objects-of-another-instance-in-typed-slots.ir.
# The objects of both instances have the same shapes. A method runs with the variables of the instance that made its object, whoever calls it, so `mark` tells whose code answered; and each instance has guards, classes and closures of its own.
# Each function does one deed to a value that may be the other instance's, in a loop, where a guess pays: behind a test of the shape a method is entered without its function object, behind the guard of the class of the instance that runs.
# So the code of a ShapeTest asks for the instance too, as that of a TypeTest does, and an object of the other instance goes by name. Without that: `call 3,3 and not call 3,6`, the same out of a slot, and the old method where the other instance has replaced it.
# At the end the shell runs the same text twice itself: every answer is the same.
